    <!-- 9 EUTHANASIA -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="euthanasia">
      <span class="tag lo">Euthanasia</span>
      <h2>Ending life: sanctity vs compassion</h2>
      <p><span class="hl t">Euthanasia</span> means bringing about a gentle death to end suffering. Key distinctions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Voluntary</b> — at the person's own request; <b>non-voluntary</b> — the person cannot ask (e.g. in a coma).</li>
        <li><b>Active</b> — deliberately doing something to end life; <b>passive</b> — withdrawing or withholding burdensome treatment.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Euthanasia is currently <b>illegal in the UK</b>. Religious and non-religious people debate it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Many Christians and Muslims:</b> uphold the <b>sanctity of life</b> and oppose deliberately ending a life, though many accept <b>withdrawing burdensome treatment</b> and giving good palliative care.</li>
        <li><b>Humanists:</b> tend to weigh a person's <b>autonomy</b> and their suffering, and some support assisted dying with safeguards.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="note"><b>Sensitively:</b> arguments focus on <b>sanctity of life</b> (life is sacred, "do not kill") versus <b>quality of life and compassion</b> (reducing suffering, respecting choice).</div>
    </section>

    <!-- 10 LIFE AFTER DEATH -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="afterlife">
      <span class="tag lo">Life after death</span>
      <h2>How belief in an afterlife shapes value of life</h2>
      <p>Belief about what happens after death affects how people value <b>this</b> life. Christians and Muslims believe in life after death and <b>judgement</b>, which many say makes this life even more precious — a gift from God to be respected and lived well.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Christians:</b> believe in resurrection and judgement, then heaven or hell; this can strengthen support for the sanctity of life.</li>
        <li><b>Muslims:</b> believe in <b>Akhirah</b> (the afterlife) and the Day of Judgement, so actions in this life matter greatly.</li>
        <li><b>Humanists / atheists:</b> generally believe this life is the only one, which for many is a reason to make it count and to reduce suffering.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>Link:</b> beliefs about the afterlife feed directly into views on abortion and euthanasia — they shape how sacred a person thinks life is.</p>
    </section>

